course: dictionary
lesson: 13991
title: One name, many creatures
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the place you are in can change which meaning is right. Longlegs is rarely used alone. You will almost always meet it in the phrase daddy longlegs, so read the words around it. «We found a daddy longlegs in the garden shed.» The word daddy and the garden tell you it is an animal, not a person.
explain: Context can also tell you which animal is meant. In the UK, Ireland and Australia, a daddy longlegs is usually a crane fly. In the USA and Canada, it is often a harvestman or a cellar spider. The same name can mean different creatures, so check where the text is set before you decide.
explain: Longlegs can also be an informal nickname for a tall person with long legs. «Our new goalkeeper is a real longlegs.» The sentence is about a person, and it sounds friendly. Swap in your meaning to check: a tall person fits the sentence, but a spider does not.
fact: Longlegs is rarely used on its own; you will usually see «daddy longlegs».
fact: In the UK, Ireland and Australia, daddy longlegs often means the crane fly.
fact: In the USA and Canada, daddy longlegs usually means a harvestman or a cellar spider.
fact: Daddy longlegs are not deadly poisonous; they are harmless to people, so the scary story is a myth.
fact: As an informal nickname, «longlegs» means a tall person with long legs.
exercise: «We found a daddy longlegs in the garden shed.» In this sentence, what is a daddy longlegs? | A kind of cloud | *A long-legged creature | A tall person
exercise: In the UK, what is a daddy longlegs most often? | *A crane fly | A deadly poisonous spider | A tall goalkeeper
exercise: «Our new goalkeeper is a real longlegs.» What does longlegs mean here? | A crane fly | A poisonous spider | *A tall person with long legs
test: Are daddy longlegs deadly poisonous to people? | Yes, they are deadly poisonous | Yes, they are very dangerous | *No, they are harmless to people
test: In the USA and Canada, daddy longlegs often means which creature? | A crane fly | *A harvestman or a cellar spider | A tall goalkeeper
exam: Which meaning fits best in «Ella is such a longlegs that she reaches the top shelf without a stool.»? | A crane fly in the garden | *A tall person with long legs | A cellar spider in the bath
